+  its parameters do is claiming to answer who is calling out of nothing, and
+  the only honest sources for that answer are the caller and a runtime that
+  authenticated one. Passing a principal on, wrapping it in `[:option ...]`,
+  or returning it inside a `[:result ...]` are all fine, because in each of
+  those the principal came in through a parameter.
